    {
      "id": "zh-en-completed",
      "title": "Completed actions",
      "description": "了 for what just happened, 过 for what you've ever done",
      "theme": "verbs",
      "guide": {
        "intro": "A1 introduced 了 briefly. A2 is where it really earns its keep. There are also two siblings to learn — 过 (experience) and 还没 (not yet) — that round out talking about the past.",
        "sections": [
          { "kind": "heading", "text": "了 — completed action" },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Tack 了 onto a verb to mark that the action is finished. It's the closest thing Mandarin has to a past tense, but technically it's an aspect marker — the action is complete, not necessarily long ago."
          },
          {
            "kind": "examples",
            "rows": [
              { "source": "我 吃 饭。", "pinyin": "Wǒ chī fàn.", "translation": "I am eating." },
              { "source": "我 吃 了 饭。", "pinyin": "Wǒ chī le fàn.", "translation": "I ate / I have eaten." },
              { "source": "他 来 了。", "pinyin": "Tā lái le.", "translation": "He came / he's here." }
            ]
          },
          { "kind": "heading", "text": "Negation: 还没 (not yet)" },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Don't pair 了 with 不/没. To say \"haven't done it\", drop 了 and use 还没 (hái méi):"
          },
          {
            "kind": "examples",
            "rows": [
              { "source": "我 还没 吃。", "pinyin": "Wǒ hái méi chī.", "translation": "I haven't eaten yet." },
              { "source": "他 还没 来。", "pinyin": "Tā hái méi lái.", "translation": "He hasn't come yet." }
            ]
          },
          { "kind": "heading", "text": "过 — experience marker" },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "过 (guò) tags a verb as \"have you ever done this in your life?\" — it's about experience, not completion. Compare:"
          },
          {
            "kind": "examples",
            "rows": [
              { "source": "我 吃 过 北京 烤鸭。", "pinyin": "Wǒ chī guo Běijīng kǎoyā.", "translation": "I have eaten Peking duck (sometime)." },
              { "source": "我 吃 了 北京 烤鸭。", "pinyin": "Wǒ chī le Běijīng kǎoyā.", "translation": "I ate Peking duck (just now)." }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "callout",
            "tone": "tip",
            "text": "Rule of thumb: 了 = the action is wrapped up. 过 = at some point in your life this happened. They occasionally co-occur but you'll mostly pick one."
          }
        ]
      },
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "zh-en-completed-1",
