    {
      "id": "zh-en-compare",
      "title": "Comparisons",
      "description": "A is bigger than B — the 比 pattern",
      "theme": "basics",
      "guide": {
        "intro": "English uses \"-er\" or \"more\" for comparisons. Mandarin uses 比 (bǐ) — a single particle that does the same job, with a fixed word order: A 比 B + adjective.",
        "sections": [
          { "kind": "heading", "text": "Basic pattern: A 比 B + adjective" },
          {
            "kind": "examples",
            "rows": [
              { "source": "我 比 他 高。", "pinyin": "Wǒ bǐ tā gāo.", "translation": "I am taller than him." },
              { "source": "苹果 比 香蕉 便宜。", "pinyin": "Píngguǒ bǐ xiāngjiāo piányi.", "translation": "Apples are cheaper than bananas." },
              { "source": "今天 比 昨天 热。", "pinyin": "Jīntiān bǐ zuótiān rè.", "translation": "Today is hotter than yesterday." }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "callout",
            "tone": "warn",
            "text": "Don't add 很 / 不 / 是 to a 比 sentence. \"我 比 他 很 高\" is wrong — drop 很. The comparison itself does the work."
          },
          { "kind": "heading", "text": "Even more: 更" },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Add 更 (gèng, \"even more\") before the adjective when comparing to an already-strong baseline:"
          },
          {
            "kind": "examples",
            "rows": [
              { "source": "他 比 我 更 高。", "pinyin": "Tā bǐ wǒ gèng gāo.", "translation": "He is even taller than me." }
            ]
          },
          { "kind": "heading", "text": "The most: 最" },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "最 (zuì) before an adjective means \"the most\". No 比 needed — it's a superlative."
          },
          {
            "kind": "examples",
            "rows": [
              { "source": "他 最 高。", "pinyin": "Tā zuì gāo.", "translation": "He is the tallest." },
              { "source": "我 最 喜欢 茶。", "pinyin": "Wǒ zuì xǐhuan chá.", "translation": "I like tea the most." }
            ]
          },
          { "kind": "heading", "text": "Negative: A 没有 B + adjective" },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "To say \"A is NOT as ___ as B\", flip to 没有 (méi yǒu, \"doesn't have\"):"
          },
          {
            "kind": "examples",
            "rows": [
              { "source": "我 没有 他 高。", "pinyin": "Wǒ méi yǒu tā gāo.", "translation": "I am not as tall as him." }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "zh-en-compare-1",
          "title": "A 比 B",
          "description": "Saying X is more ___ than Y",
          "theme": "basics",
          "xp": 16,
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "cm1-1",
              "type": "multiple_choice",
              "prompt": "What does \"我 比 他 高\" mean?",
              "options": ["He is taller than me", "I am taller than him", "I am as tall as him", "I am not as tall as him"],
              "answer": "I am taller than him"
            },
            {
              "id": "cm1-2",
              "type": "tap_words_in_order",
              "prompt": "Build \"Apples are cheaper than bananas\"",
              "answer": "苹果 比 香蕉 便宜",
              "bank": ["苹果", "比", "香蕉", "便宜", "贵", "更"]
            },
            {
              "id": "cm1-3",
              "type": "multiple_choice",
              "prompt": "Which is correct for \"Today is hotter than yesterday\"?",
              "options": ["今天 比 昨天 热", "今天 很 比 昨天 热", "今天 不 热 昨天", "昨天 比 今天 热"],
              "answer": "今天 比 昨天 热"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "zh-en-compare-2",
          "title": "Even more (更)",
          "description": "Stacking the comparison",
          "theme": "basics",
          "xp": 14,
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "cm2-1",
              "type": "multiple_choice",
              "prompt": "What does \"更\" (gèng) mean?",
              "options": ["The most", "Even more", "Already", "Very"],
              "answer": "Even more"
            },
            {
              "id": "cm2-2",
